<p class="muted">A few things tend to come through on careful listening. The <code>small-music</code> model is remarkably capable for 459M parameters and generates in well under a second on a laptop, but it can smear fast transients and thin out the stereo field. <code>medium</code> firms up the low end and the rhythmic grid. <code>large</code> usually has the cleanest high frequencies and the most convincing room sound. The gaps are smaller than the 6× parameter spread might suggest — a testament to how much work the SAME latent is doing before diffusion even starts.</p>

